WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.936
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with David Letterman.

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.705
And we showed a clip.
-My goodness. The band.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.873
That's so nice
to hear live music.

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:10.877
It's so great to be this close
to live music every night.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.612
-I probably take it
for granted.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.581
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.816
-It's something
that I truly missed

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.684
when I first left the old show.

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:20.019
This is lovely.

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.387
-It's great to have them back.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:22.822
It's great to be in a room
with them, absolutely.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.124
-Because what I've learned --

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.791
And this probably
doesn't happen in your case.

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:29.796
Even when the show
that I did blew,

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:33.500
the audience would get
great live music.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.867
Free.

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:36.369
-Yeah, not a bad trade-off.
-Yeah.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.703
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:39.939
-Now, Elevator Races.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:43.042
The representational clip
available.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.443
-Yeah,
the representational clip.

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:47.480
How about Bob Costas there?
-Bob Costas.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.783
There's a new YouTube channel
that launched today

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:52.084
that basically
has the full archives

00:00:52.084 --> 00:00:53.352
of your time on the show.

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:56.356
And it is -- You can spend
a lot of time on it.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:59.426
I was watching
world's largest vase.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:02.128
-Oh, the world's largest vase.
-Yeah.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.697
-First of all, thank you for
mentioning the YouTube thing.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.634
You know,
you get the YouTube app.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.903
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.106
And so you get to see things
that were also

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:15.775
spreading misinformation
about the vaccine.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.476
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:20.079
But the world's largest vase,

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.981
it was something
we had on the show.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.583
And I don't know the origin.
I don't know where it came from.

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:27.286
But it was documented
as the world's largest vase.

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:28.688
And it came to New York City.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.356
And you're thinking,
"Oh, that's cute."

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.726
A week -- an entire week,
five shows, every night.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:37.030
The world's largest vase.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.298
On the Friday night,
the last night of the show,

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:43.135
or Thursday night,
whatever it was, we had --

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:47.307
the world's largest vase
addressed the studio audience.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.507
-Yeah.

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.977
-And called for
a peaceful world.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.344
-Yeah.

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:54.580
-And there was also a book
that had been published.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.117
It was children's letters
to the world's largest vase.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.052
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:03.789
And for some reason,
we all loved that.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:07.126
And I think that --
It was tickling to think that,

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.028
"Yeah, you want
to watch some TV?

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.397
Turn on NBC.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.532
It's the world's largest vase.

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:15.969
Enjoy it, everybody!"

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.703
-Now, it's not always
fun and games.

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:20.473
This is a photo of Jack Hanna.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.341
Made many appearances
on your show.

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:24.577
-Countless.
-But this is a day

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.011
that did not go
particularly well.

00:02:26.011 --> 00:02:27.980
You want to tell us
what's happening in that photo?

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.348
-You know,
I had forgotten about this.

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:31.784
Jack, for those of you
who may --

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:34.854
Anyway, I'll tell you, was a
tremendous guy, a very nice guy.

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:38.257
And he was the director
of the Columbus zoo

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.025
for years and years and years.

00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:42.262
And like two or three times
a year --

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:44.297
Do you have a guy
that comes on with animals?

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.499
-We don't have an animal guy.
-What?!

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.900
-Yeah.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:51.303
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:53.872
-Wait a minute!
You don't have an animal guy?!

00:02:53.872 --> 00:02:56.842
-I can tell you --
We don't have an animal guy.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:59.378
-Wow!
-Yeah.

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:01.013
-What are you doin' here?!

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:04.049
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:08.654
Well, anyway -- So, he would
bring wild and exotic

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:13.426
and unregistered animals
onto the show,

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:16.162
and they would be, you know,
like 40-foot snakes,

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:19.865
and we'd have bald eagles
and condors

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:22.201
and 1,000-year-old turtles

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:25.671
and all kinds of --
well, zoo animals, you know.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:28.141
-Yeah.
-And Jack would --

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.742
As it turned out,
two or three shows in,

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.078
we realized Jack knew nothing
about animals.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.446
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.649
But he had
his little safari suit on.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:39.319
And I was talking to Jack
about a year ago,

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:41.854
and I had completely
forgotten about this.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:45.324
And this is Jack there.

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:47.994
And that's his head shot.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.763
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:54.167
And toward the end
of the segment, the beaver --

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.135
They have long teeth.
-Famously.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.137
-Because they're constantly
eating wood.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.739
Famously. That's right.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:03.175
Without that,
they'd be nothing.

00:04:03.175 --> 00:04:06.712
And the beaver punctured Jack

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:09.081
right between the index finger
and the thumb.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:13.352
And I'm told that that's
a source of gushing blood.

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:14.787
Thank you, Jack.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.055
Columbus Zoo, director
of the Columbus Zoo.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.290
Jack goes backstage,
and he's hemorrhaging.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.693
And he's got his hand
right here.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:26.366
And we were not far from
a hospital down south of here.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.200
And Jack said, "No, no, no, no."

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.503
Jack didn't want to -- He didn't
want to call attention.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:33.906
He was afraid
he would embarrass the show.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.341
I never had that fear.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.877
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:41.981
So I became inured to that.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.549
Jack walks into the --
and nobody --

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.817
You couldn't give him a ride.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.652
Jack walks into
the emergency room,

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:48.955
and the woman,
or the attendant,

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:52.958
whomever it was at the desk,
picks up the emergency phone,

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:56.662
because Jack's now covered
with blood in his abdomen.

00:04:56.662 --> 00:05:00.433
"Gunshot victim! Gunshot victim!
Gunshot victim!" Click.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:04.437
Now everybody in the hospital
comes running out toward Jack.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.639
And they said,
"Where were you shot?"

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.773
This and that.

00:05:07.773 --> 00:05:09.241
And Jack said,
"No, no, I wasn't shot.

00:05:09.241 --> 00:05:10.910
I was bitten by a beaver."

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.145
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:16.282
And now the police hear that --

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:18.184
Now, this is a real violation,

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:20.052
because the police come over
and they say,

00:05:20.052 --> 00:05:23.856
"You know, there are no beaver
in New York, sir."

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.726
Because they think they got --
Who knows what they got?

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:29.595
And he said, "No, no, no, no,
no, no, no, the beaver is mine."

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:30.963
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:33.332
And the police said,
"You're not allowed --

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.701
It's illegal to have a beaver
in New York City!"

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:36.869
-Sure.
-Yeah.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:39.805
So he goes from being bitten
by the beaver,

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.574
mistaken as a gunshot victim,

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:46.145
to arguing with the police about
what he is doing with a beaver.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.946
And the whole time, the poor man

00:05:47.946 --> 00:05:50.949
lost like a quart of blood
over the deal.

00:05:50.949 --> 00:05:52.652
That's why you need
an animal guy.

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:53.752
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:55.120
-That's quite a sales pitch.
-Yeah.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.889
-That's quite a sales pitch.
-Get one of those guys.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:59.058
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Now, I should note,

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.960
people couldn't see it
when we showed

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.362
that clip of your show.

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.929
You had no interest
in watching it.

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:05.431
-Yeah, that's correct.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:08.000
-It's safe to say you will not
be visiting your YouTube page.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.470
-No, not unless
it's part of a rendition.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.740
-Now, does your --
We also talked about your son.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.775
You know, like, my kids
will have the same thing

00:06:16.775 --> 00:06:18.343
when they get a little older.

00:06:18.343 --> 00:06:20.646
-I love the fact that you have
three kids those ages.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.248
I think that's just delightful.

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:24.884
And you folks
probably have kids, eh?

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:27.086
-Yeah, I think there's probably
some parents out there tonight.

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:28.854
-I mean,
even when it gets edgy,

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:30.222
it's still the best, isn't it?

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:31.857
I mean, my goodness.
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:34.026
-No, I was just going to ask.
Does your son, Harry --

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.362
does he enjoy watching
old clips of his dad?

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:38.864
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:38.864 --> 00:06:41.567
Yeah, I don't think he enjoys
seeing me in person.

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:46.238
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.238 --> 00:06:49.875
I am so upset with Harry because
I have been sitting on a story,

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:52.311
Seth, since the summer.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:54.046
And I thought,
if somebody is nice enough

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:57.850
to invite me on a talk show,
I am ready to go.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.519
And so I have been rehearsing it
and going over it

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:02.789
and over it in my head,
beat by beat.

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:05.024
And last night,
I said to Harry, I said,

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.759
"I'm going to be
on the 'Seth Meyers' show.

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.760
Is it okay
if I tell this story?"

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.830
[Silly voice]
"I'd really rather you didn't."

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.466
[Normal voice] Voices.

00:07:14.466 --> 00:07:16.735
And I said, "No, no, I mean,
I'm not going to say anything --

00:07:16.735 --> 00:07:18.337
It's all about me.
It's not going to --

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:21.040
"No, please don't tell
that story."

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.643
So I honor that.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:24.977
I'm not going to tell the story.

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:27.013
I'll just give you
the highlights.

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:28.848
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:31.083
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:34.353
Thank you.

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:36.421
Have you ever been
knocked unconscious?

00:07:36.421 --> 00:07:37.623
-No.

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:39.291
-Neither had I.
Until this summer.

00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:40.593
-Wow!
-Yeah.

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:42.628
Have you ever ridden
in an ambulance?

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:43.762
-Yes.
-Really?

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:45.297
-Yeah.
-What was that?

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.333
-Well, my --
-Oh, is this in the lobby?

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:49.235
-Yeah, my kid was born
in the lobby,

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:51.270
and then they still make you
go to the hospital.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.705
-Wow! Wow!
-But it's the best --

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.840
I mean, the best way
to ride in an ambulance

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.276
is with a baby who's already
been born and is healthy.

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:59.045
You know,
then it's just a joy ride.

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:00.846
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:02.481
Yours was probably less so.

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:05.151
-Yeah, my whole story
is less so, thanks to you.

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:07.853
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:10.456
-Harry called me and said,
"Tell yours."

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.391
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:19.165
-That little weasel!

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.266
But over the Christmas holidays,

00:08:21.266 --> 00:08:23.569
here's a story that he did --
-Oh, he signed off on one.

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:27.073
-Yeah, greenlight this one.

00:08:27.073 --> 00:08:30.175
He's at that age where
I just don't do anything

00:08:30.175 --> 00:08:31.944
that makes sense to him.

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:34.780
And so I said, "Harry."
We had a Christmas tree,

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.082
and there was no way
to water it,

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:37.916
and I figured out,
let's go to the hardware store

00:08:37.916 --> 00:08:39.752
and get a length
of plastic tube.

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:42.021
That way, you just pour the
water in the plastic tube,

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:43.589
it goes into
the Christmas tree.

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:47.259
Bang, zoom.
I'm like Phil Swift.

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:50.363
And so I said, "Harry, tomorrow
let's go to the hardware store."

00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:52.264
"Uh, maybe."

00:08:52.264 --> 00:08:54.666
Now, 18-year-olds, you know,
"maybe" means "no."

00:08:54.666 --> 00:08:56.669
So, the next day,
"So, how do you feel

00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:58.337
about that trip
to the hardware...?"

00:08:58.337 --> 00:09:01.106
"I got stuff to do."
Again it means "no."

00:09:01.106 --> 00:09:03.309
He has nothing to do.

00:09:03.309 --> 00:09:05.577
Later in the day, before
the hardware store closes --

00:09:05.577 --> 00:09:08.481
and this is -- It was touching
because you often wonder,

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:11.784
"Does my kid worry
about my health?"

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:13.552
And this was a moment
when I realized

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:14.953
he did worry about my health.

00:09:14.953 --> 00:09:16.589
Because I said to him,

00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:18.724
"Harry, I'm tired of
asking you about this.

00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:21.460
The hardware store closes
in about a half an hour.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.195
Will you go with me
to the hardware store

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:26.866
to buy the hose
so we can water the tree?"

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:28.567
"I really don't want to go,

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:31.537
but I know if I don't,
your head will explode."

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:33.939
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.939 --> 00:09:38.844
So I realized,
"Oh, he does care about me."

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:40.246
God bless Dad.

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.013
[ Applause ]

00:09:42.013 --> 00:09:45.551
-Well, he's not alone.

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:47.286
We all care about you.
-Aw. You're so kind.

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:48.720
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:49.888
-Oh, no, thank you.

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:52.091
-This is a really nice
celebration.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:53.992
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Very nice of you.

00:09:53.992 --> 00:09:56.495
-You know, I think --

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:58.163
I think
you and I share something.

00:09:58.163 --> 00:09:59.865
We're maybe not a lot
for fanfare,

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:02.868
but this is a holiday of sorts.

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:04.469
So you take these

00:10:04.469 --> 00:10:06.972
and you point it away from
your face and you turn it.

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:08.406
You see the arrows?
-Mm-hmm.

00:10:08.406 --> 00:10:09.808
-And we're gonna turn it.

00:10:09.808 --> 00:10:11.577
-This is not going to be
another trip to the hospital?

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:12.811
-No, no, no.
I already watched it.

00:10:12.811 --> 00:10:14.279
This is our celebratory --

00:10:14.279 --> 00:10:16.448
Just turn it and -- Oh, my God.
It's harder than I thought.

00:10:16.448 --> 00:10:17.817
We got to get Jenny out here.

00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:20.385
[ Laughter ]

00:10:20.385 --> 00:10:21.620
Oh. Here we go.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.589
-That was dazzling.
-Here it goes.

00:10:23.589 --> 00:10:25.557
-Oh. Wait a minute.

00:10:25.557 --> 00:10:28.393
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:28.393 --> 00:10:31.197
-They really haven't done us
any favors.

00:10:31.197 --> 00:10:36.435
Well, hopefully by
the 41st anniversary...

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:37.836
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:39.938
You're going the wrong --
You got to go with the arrows.

